@@ opening_story
Amara|David. Come to the house. Ethan is gone.
David|I am coming. Are you somewhere safe?
Amara|I saw Victor carrying him. I called his name and the lights went out.
David|Tell me which door you are standing beside.
Amara|The back door. It is still bolted. The gate is locked. I don't understand how he left.
David|Stay there. Don't go into the rain looking by yourself.
Amara|Bring him back. Please, David. Save the baby. Whatever happens, make sure he comes back alive.
David|I am at the gate. Let me in, Amara.
@@ chapter01
Detective Morris|The search starts now. Amara, tell me what you saw. David, keep the original messages and stay with her.
Amara|He was beside the nursery. Ethan's blue sleeve was against his coat.
David|Did you see his face before the lights failed?
Amara|Yes. Do not ask me that because the doors are locked.
David|I am asking so we keep what you saw separate from what we still need to explain.
Amara|Then write this first. I saw Victor take my son.
@@ season01
David|The gate has not been forced.
Amara|You can stop looking at me when you say that.
David|I am not doubting you. I am doubting the route we assumed he used.
Amara|There was a delivery worker here yesterday. His wife keeps calling him.
David|We can establish where he was without blaming him for being nearby.
@@ chapter02
Victor|My money or Ethan.
Amara|He is not your son. That money is not yours.
Victor|Then decide which one you want to keep.
David|He ended the call. My recording started too late.
Amara|I thought hearing his voice would make this easier to prove. Now I can only hear what he said.
@@ season02
David|When he says money, what does he mean?
Amara|Ethan's father left a portion of his wealth for him. Victor calls it his reward.
David|For what?
Amara|For being near me when something good happened. That is how he counts other people's lives.
David|We keep the call record and what you remember. We won't let his word become the name of a real debt.
@@ season03
David|The message mentions the cupboard beside the nursery.
Amara|It is behind the door. You cannot see it from the garden.
David|Then its sender knows something about the inside of the house.
Amara|Can that take us to him?
David|It gives us a claim we can test. I won't pretend it gives us a location yet.
@@ chapter03
Amara|I used to sell breakfast before sunrise, then deliver parcels after lunch.
David|Was Victor working with you?
Amara|He said his aura brought the customers. Once I bought him shoes and he thanked his luck.
David|Not you?
Amara|I kept waiting for it. I don't know why that is the part I remember now.
@@ season04
Detective Morris|The worker is cleared. I have spoken to his family. We will not use a frightened man's name to make this case look further along.
David|The trace does not belong to the person who left it here.
Amara|Then the worker did not come back that morning?
David|No. Someone wanted us to think he had.
Amara|Tell his wife before she hears another rumour.
David|We will keep the planted material. Finding the lie has told us what someone wanted us to do.
@@ chapter04
David|I thought the timestamps gave us the route. I was wrong.
Amara|Ethan wakes when the pump starts. I used to turn it off early.
David|The pump?
Amara|The sound before I saw Victor. I thought it was the storm.
David|That is not in the log. Show me where you normally switch it off.
@@ season05
Amara|Sometimes I think Victor killed Ethan's father too.
David|What happened that made you think it?
Amara|He died suddenly. Nobody would answer me. Then Victor arrived as if a place had become vacant.
David|We will not dismiss the question. We also cannot call it answered.
Amara|I know. Being frightened of him does not give me proof.
@@ season06
Detective Morris|I have taken the witness's account. We will protect the person and preserve the original statement.
David|The witness remembers a service vehicle before the rain became heavy.
Amara|Did they see Ethan?
David|No. We should not put that into their account.
Amara|Then tell me what they did see.
David|A company mark and a staff coat. Both are things we can check. The witness will remain available.
@@ chapter05
Amara|Victor came here after the funeral. He said we could start again.
David|What did you tell him?
Amara|That I would rather remain unmarried than return to him.
Victor|Yet you found another man soon enough.
Amara|You heard my refusal. You just decided it could not be real.
@@ season07
David|The service company was used by Adrian's estate office.
Amara|They arranged repairs before we moved in.
David|Was anyone supposed to keep access afterward?
Amara|Not that I knew. I was given keys, not a list of permissions.
David|Then we need the arrangement behind the repairs, not only the name on the van.
@@ season08
Amara|Someone called to tell me grief can make a person see things.
David|What did you say?
Amara|That grief did not put a blue sleeve against Victor's coat.
David|The marks beside the internal doorway support your account.
Amara|I want them to stop asking me whether I saw him and start asking how he got through.
@@ chapter06
David|There is a damaged image from inside the property.
Amara|Another picture that ends before the part we need?
David|The corner near the service passage may still be recoverable. That is the detail worth restoring.
Amara|Then work on the doorway. Don't spend our time making the curtains clearer.
@@ season09
David|The restored section shows Victor beside the internal passage.
Amara|That is the coat. That is what I saw.
David|We have corroboration of his presence now.
Amara|But the picture cannot tell us who opened the way for him.
David|No. We compare it with the household access record next.
@@ season10
David|There is an authorised entry during the time you were asleep.
Amara|Whose?
David|It bears your name.
Amara|I did not open anything for him.
David|Then the next question is how somebody used permission that looked like yours.
